sentences.l:
Cut off sagehood, throw away cleverness —
the people profit a hundredfold;
cut off humaneness, throw away rightness —
the people return to filial devotion and parental love;
cut off contrivance, throw away gain —
robbers and brigands, none to be had.
These three, taken as a form of words, are not enough;
so cause [them] to have something to attach to:
show the undyed silk, hold the uncarved block,
make self-interest small, make desires few.
